<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Palatinate-Veldenz</h1><p class="st-meta">1543 CE – 1694 CE · capital Lauterecken</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Wittelsbach duchy on the Glan and in the northern Vosges, created in 1543 for a younger branch of the Zweibrücken line.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>By the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marburg">Marburg</a> in 1543, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/count-palatine">Count Palatine</a> Rupert, uncle and former guardian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfgang-count-palatine-of-zweibrucken">Duke Wolfgang of Palatinate-Zweibrücken</a>, received the old <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-veldenz">County of Veldenz</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lauterecken">Lauterecken</a> and lands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vosges">Vosges</a>, founding the line of Palatinate-Veldenz.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dukes ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lauterecken">Lauterecken</a> and from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-petite-pierre">Lützelstein</a> (La Petite-Pierre) in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vosges">Vosges</a>, a scattered and poor territory of farming villages. They were Lutheran, and Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-john-i-count-palatine-of-veldenz">George John</a> founded the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalsbourg">Phalsbourg</a> in 1570. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reunions">Reunions</a>, which claimed the Vosges lands for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> after 1680, devastated the little state.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-louis-count-palatine-of-veldenz">Leopold Louis</a> died without male heirs in 1694, a long inheritance dispute followed among the Palatine branches. It was settled only in 1733, when the lands were shared among the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/electoral-palatinate">Electoral Palatinate</a> and other Wittelsbach lines.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/palatinate-veldenz.jpg" alt="Palatinate-Veldenz" width="257" height="193"><figcaption>Image: Gustav Droysen; derivative work by Beckstet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rheingraf_1400.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1543 CE – 1694 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lauterecken</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Rupert, George John, Leopold Louis</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pfalz-Veldenz, Palatinate-Lützelstein</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1618&amp;focus=palatinate-veldenz" aria-label="Palatinate-Veldenz on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4841 441 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Palatinate-Veldenz lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5161 697L5170 716"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5170 716h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5161 697h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5161 697h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1618&amp;focus=palatinate-veldenz">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
